#!/bin/sh
set -e
if [ "$1" = "configure" ]; then
  cat <<'MSG'

VoidFM host was installed.
Run the following as your normal user (not root) to set up and start it:

    voidfm start

Or open "VoidFM Host" from the app grid: a panel icon appears (and from
the next login it starts automatically) with start / stop / settings.

The first run creates a Python environment in ~/.local/share/voidfm
and downloads PyTorch / Chatterbox TTS (several GB).
MSG
fi
exit 0
